    <body>
      <div xml:id="gom-sir29">
        <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e98">Caput 29</head>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e100">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e102">Versus 5</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e104">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e106" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_5@1-2">Donec accipiant.</quote>
            <ref xml:id="gom-sir29-Rd1e109"><name xml:id="gom-sir29-Nd1e110" ref="#RabanusMaurus">RAB.</name></ref>
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e113">Hujusmodi morbum melius curat timor Dei. Qui enim Deum <pb ed="#P" n="1214A"/> quasi semper praesentem pertimescit, neminem fraudare intendit.</quote>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e120">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e122">Versus 10</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e124">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e126" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_10@1-1">Multis,</quote>
            etc.
            <ref xml:id="gom-sir29-Rd1e129"><name xml:id="gom-sir29-Nd1e130" ref="#RabanusMaurus">ID.</name></ref>
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e133">Illos notat, qui neminem laedere volunt, sed prae timore periturarum rerum prodesse nolunt. Contra quos dicitur: <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e135" source="http://scta.info/resource/mt6_19@1-6">Nolite thesaurizare vobis thesauros in terra</quote>.</quote>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e141">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e143">Versus 12</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e145">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e147" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_12@1-2">Propter mandatum.</quote>
            Omnibus indigentibus misericordia est facienda, nec pro avaritia charitas proximi amittenda.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e152">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e154">Versus 13</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e156">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e158" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_13@7-9">Et non abscondas.</quote>
            Qui enim viderit fratrem suum necesse habere, et clauserit viscera sua ab eo, quomodo charitas Dei manet in eo?
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e164">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e166">Versus 18</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e168">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e170" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_18@1-3">Super scutum potentis,</quote>
            etc. Magis valet eleemosyna contra jacula inimici, quam <pb ed="#P" n="1214B"/> arma terrena: quia haec dubiam, illa certissimam parit victoriam, ut absorbeatur mors in victoria.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e177">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e179">Versus 23</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e181">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e183" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_23">Qui perdiderit,</quote>
            <!-- check: lemma not matched to verse text -->
            etc. Id est, qui unitatem fidei, et sinceritatem legis non custodit, sed implicatur erroribus variis.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e190">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e192">Versus 20</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e194">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e196" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_20@1-2">Gratiam fidejussoris,</quote>
            etc. Doctorem scilicet qui pro fide et bonis operibus promittit vitam aeternam. Haec sententia Pelagium reprehendit qui liberum arbitrium gratiae praeponit, cum per solam gratiam liberentur electi.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e201">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e203">Versus 27</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e205">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e207" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_27@1-2">Recupera proximum.</quote>
            Consulit, ut secundum vires proximo praebeas solatium, et sic tibi praevideas, ne in laqueum cadas.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e212">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e214">Versus 28</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e216">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e218" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_28@1-2">Initium vitae,</quote>
            etc.
            <ref xml:id="gom-sir29-Rd1e221"><name xml:id="gom-sir29-Nd1e222" ref="#RabanusMaurus">RAB.</name></ref>
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e225"><seg type="qs">Fragilitatem, et hospitalitatem et honestatem docet, etc., <pb ed="#P" n="1214C"/></seg> usque ad <seg type="qs">et Dominus primis parentibus pelliceas tunicas post peccatum fecit.</seg></quote>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e235">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e237">Versus 29</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e239">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e241" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_29@1-3">Melior est victus pauperis,</quote>
            etc. Ad litteram. Melius est tenuem victum sub vili tugurio sumere in securitate, quam splendidas epulas cum fatigatione in incertis locis quaerere.
          </p>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e245">
            <ref xml:id="gom-sir29-Rd1e247" type="lemma" subtype="implied" target="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_29@1-3"/>
            <ref xml:id="gom-sir29-Rd1e249"><name xml:id="gom-sir29-Nd1e250" ref="#RabanusMaurus">ID.</name></ref>
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e253"><seg type="qs">Allegorice. Melior est victus</seg>, etc., usque ad <seg type="qs">ubi labor et superflua cura.</seg></quote>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e263">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e265">Versus 30</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e267">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e269" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_30@2-2">Minimum.</quote>
            <ref xml:id="gom-sir29-Rd1e272"><name xml:id="gom-sir29-Nd1e273" ref="#RabanusMaurus">ID.</name></ref>
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e276"><seg type="qs">Sufficiat tibi quod habes</seg>, etc., usque ad <seg type="qs">melius est nomen bonum quam deliciae multae.</seg></quote>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e285">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e287">Versus 33</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e289">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e291" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_33@1-1">Transi.</quote>
            Quasi: Qui alieno delectaris hospitio, redi ad propria, et de labore tuo te et alios pasce. Noli de aliena domo pastum tibi superfluum quaerere. Sufficit tibi susceptio proximorum.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir29-Dd1e296">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir29-Hd1e298">Versus 35</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir29-d1e300">
            <pb ed="#P" n="1214D"/>
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e304" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir29_35@9-9">Improperium.</quote>
            <ref xml:id="gom-sir29-Rd1e307"><name xml:id="gom-sir29-Nd1e308" ref="#RabanusMaurus">RAB.</name></ref>
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir29-Qd1e311"><seg type="qs">Mystice autem monetur vir ecclesiasticus</seg>, etc., usque ad <seg type="qs">in futuro autem examine aeternum confusionis improperium sustineat.</seg></quote>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </body>
